From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:48:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winex11, win32u: a window the window manager moved onto a new
 screen is on it.

When a monitor goes, the window manager moves the windows on it onto one
that is still there, before this side has heard of the change.  A window
put somewhere off the screen this side still knew was taken to have been
moved out of sight on purpose: the Win32 side was not told, and every later
move of the window was offset by the same amount on its way to the X
server.  Turned from landscape to portrait, the shadow windows around Word
went to the bottom of the screen, 600 pixels to the left of their windows,
and Word was then told that is where they were.

An offset like that is now only kept while the place the window manager put
the window is still off the screen.  And after a display change every
visible window is brought up to date with the host, as windows being fitted
to the new screen already were, so a place on the new screen is passed on
once this side knows the new screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 82486d6bca83a7baab63c805aa3bc75cc59cc9ff)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/window.c b/dlls/win32u/window.c
index 4915bb3fa83..a0dd77d3a71 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -5091,7 +5091,12 @@ static BOOL moved_off_display( HWND hwnd, const RECT *old_monitors, const RECT *
 
 /* Each window is put right in its own thread, which is where its window
  * procedure answers WM_GETMINMAXINFO.  The monitors it may have been on are
- * those of the configuration before the change, in system DPI. */
+ * those of the configuration before the change, in system DPI.
+ *
+ * Every other window is brought up to date with the host as well: the window
+ * manager moves windows onto the new monitors before this side has heard of
+ * them, and a place on the new screen that is off the old one was taken for
+ * the window being put out of sight, and not passed on. */
 void fit_windows_to_display( const RECT *old_monitors, const RECT *old_work, UINT old_count )
 {
     POINT origin = {0};
@@ -5109,9 +5114,12 @@ void fit_windows_to_display( const RECT *old_monitors, const RECT *old_work, UIN
 
         how = (style & WS_MAXIMIZE) ? FIT_MAXIMIZED : 0;
         if (moved_off_display( list[i], old_monitors, old_work, old_count, &origin )) how |= FIT_RESCUE;
-        if (!how) continue;
 
-        if (is_current_thread_window( list[i] )) fit_window_to_display( list[i], how, origin );
+        if (is_current_thread_window( list[i] ))
+        {
+            if (how) fit_window_to_display( list[i], how, origin );
+            update_window_state( list[i] );
+        }
         else NtUserPostMessage( list[i], WM_WINE_UPDATEWINDOWSTATE, how, MAKELPARAM( origin.x, origin.y ));
     }
 
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index 7ff2c51ffca..c20680c2122 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -2291,6 +2291,9 @@ static void sync_window_position( struct x11drv_win_data *data, UINT swp_flags,
 
     /* if the window has been moved offscreen by the window manager, we didn't tell the Win32 side about it */
     window_rect = window_rect_from_visible( old_rects, data->desired_state.rect );
+    /* unless it was only off a screen that has changed since: the window manager moves windows
+     * onto the new monitors before this side knows of them, and there it is on the screen */
+    if (data->is_offscreen && is_window_rect_mapped( &window_rect )) data->is_offscreen = FALSE;
     if (data->is_offscreen) OffsetRect( &new_rect, window_rect.left - old_rects->window.left,
                                         window_rect.top - old_rects->window.top );
 
